# Enumerated data types (ed.3 6.4.4.1 / ed.2 2.3.3.1): the default initial
# value of an enumerated variable is the first value of the type (RED);
# values can be assigned, compared for equality, and used as CASE labels.
#   cycle 0: pick = -1 leaves c at its initial RED; prev = RED too.
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs: pick
outputs: code is_green same
status: conformant
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.3 6.4.4.1 (enumerated data types), 6.4.4.4 (default initial value), 7.3.3.3.3 (CASE)
---
0 pick=-1 => code=1 is_green=FALSE same=TRUE
1 pick=1  => code=2 is_green=TRUE  same=FALSE
2 pick=1  => code=2 is_green=TRUE  same=TRUE
3 pick=2  => code=3 is_green=FALSE same=FALSE
4 pick=0  => code=1 is_green=FALSE same=FALSE
5 pick=7  => code=1 is_green=FALSE same=TRUE
